:bust_in_silhouette: **anthony@whitford.com** &nbsp; :clock8: Aug 12, 2010 at 07:05 UTC

delombok code on Windows ends up with a different end-of-line convention for the first line (the comment that says, &quot;Generated by delombok ...&quot;) and every other line.  It is because it is hard coded to be LF (\n) for the first line, but then the Sun code takes care of the rest being appropriately native (CR/LF).

I suggest changing this:

public void print(Writer out) throws IOException {
  if (!changed) {
    JavaFileObject sourceFile = compilationUnit.getSourceFile();
    if (sourceFile != null) {
      out.write(sourceFile.getCharContent(true).toString());
      return;
    }
  }

  out.write(&quot;// Generated by delombok at &quot; + new Date() + &quot;\n&quot;);
  compilationUnit.accept(new PrettyCommentsPrinter(out, compilationUnit, comments));
}

to be:

public void print(PrintWriter out) throws IOException {
  if (!changed) {
    JavaFileObject sourceFile = compilationUnit.getSourceFile();
    if (sourceFile != null) {
      out.write(sourceFile.getCharContent(true).toString());
      return;
    }
  }

  out.println(&quot;// Generated by delombok at &quot; + new Date());
  compilationUnit.accept(new PrettyCommentsPrinter(out, compilationUnit, comments));
}

In other words, replace the Writer with a PrintWriter, then say out.println instead of out.write, and note that then you can drop the hard-coded line feed (\n).

