Sounds like a plan. Instead of 'new A(t);' we suggest we do this instead:

catch (Throwable t) {
    if (t instanceof WrapperException) throw (WrapperException) t;
    if (t instanceof RuntimeException) throw (RuntimeException) t;
    WrapperException newEx = new WrapperException();
    newEx.initCause(t);
    throw newEx;
}

and instead of:

@ WrapExceptions(wrapper=WrapperException.class), we'll also add an option to specify which exceptions ought to be wrapped (which defaults to Throwable).

