I'd like to propose an extension to the @ RequiredArgsConstructor annotation. Here's the rationale:

When creating components for dependency injection, required types should be exposed as constructor arguments. For some containers (e.g. Spring) the constructor needs to be annotated with a marker annotation (in the case of Spring @ Autowired or @ Inject). Thus an example class would look like this:

class MyComponent {

  private final MyDependency dependency;

  @ Inject
  public MyComponent(MyDependency dependency) {
    this.dependency = dependency;
  }
}

The requirement to annotate the constructor currently rules out the usage of @ RequiredArgsConstructor. The annotation could take an array of annotation classes, the constructor generation mechanism would annotate the generated constructor with:

public @ interface RequiredArgsConstructor {

  // … current fields omitted

  Class&lt;? extends Annotation&gt;[] constructorAnnotations default {};
}

to be used like:

@ RequiredArgsConstructor(constructorAnnotations = Inject.class)
class MyComponent {
  private final MyDependency dependency;
}

