The `setClassList(Collection<String>)`` is not totally unnnecessary (and dangerous, as it creates a new collection) but it also has the unfortunate side effect of blowing up JSON deserialziation.

When this class is passed to Jackson to reconstitute from JSON, Jackson now throws an exception complaining about multiple incompatible setters.

