According to [this StackOverflow answer](http://stackoverflow.com/a/33998171/1036728), `@Tolerate` supposedly prevents lombok from not generating a method due to signature conflicts.  `@Tolerate` however does not seem to prevent this with `@Builder`'s field methods:

### Example of `@Tolerate` not working:
```java
@lombok.Builder
public class Foo {
	private final int value;

	public static void main(String[] args) {
		Foo.builder().valueAsString("42").build();
	}

	public static class FooBuilder {
		@Tolerate
		public FooBuilder value(String s) {
			return this.value(Integer.parseInt(s));
		}
	}
}
```
```
Exception in thread "main" java.lang.Error: Unresolved compilation problem: 
	The method value(String) in the type Foo.FooBuilder is not applicable for the arguments (int)

	at Foo$FooBuilder.value(Foo.java:19)
	at Foo.main(Foo.java:12)
```

### Working alternative 1:

```java
@lombok.Builder
public class Foo {
	private final int value;

	public static class FooBuilder {
		public FooBuilder valueAsString(String s) {
			return this.value(Integer.parseInt(s));
		}
	}
}
```

### Working alternative 2:

