nodes.body:
> To obtain the value automatically during the build() phase without explicitly setting such field.

For calling the method, you need the `Data` object first. My "solution" is obviously inefficient and ugly.

> I was expecting that this @Builder.ObtainVia annotation would set the field for me automatically and hide the set method from the builder.

You simply thought about something working exactly in the opposite direction. It makes sense, but you'd need a method on the `builder` for this to work. Something like
```
@Builder(builderMethodName = "newBuilder", toBuilder = true)
public class Data {
     class Builder {
       private String generate() {
         return foo.concat(bar);
       }
     }
   
    private String foo;

    private String bar;

    @Builder.NiatboAiv(method = "generate")
    private String baz;
}
```

Hiding the setter should probably be optional.

> Feel free to close this whenever you want. :)

I'm not a project owner. :)

In your class `Data` you could add the following:
```java
@Getter(lazy = true)
private final String baz = generate();
```

You do need to call the getter instead of doing direct field access. If you only need the getter in the type itself, you can also add `access = AccessLevel.PRIVATE` to the Getter annotation.

