```

I guess, this is already doable: Define `canEqual` in a common superclass (or a default method in the interface, or in both classes) like
```
protected boolean canEqual(Object other) {
    return other instanceof User;
}
```
Then add `@EqualsAndHashCode` to both classes. Take care they contain exactly the same fields, or exclude them from EQHC, so that you don't break symmetry.

PS: It doesn't really have much to do with interfaces (replace "interface" by "abstract class" in your posting to see why).

