@arvindkgs There is no difference between how lombok works and how that equals method works: If you have a field that is `null` in 2 different objects, lombok's equals method considers those fields to be 'equal'.

@amarkevich 

This is the code of `Objects.equals`:

`return (a == b) || (a != null && a.equals(b));`

Lombok generates this for you. In fact, this is __no good__, in that `Objects.equals` fails to consider 2 arrays equal if they are the same size and their components are equal (because `arr.equals` doesn't work that way), lombok gets that right.

There is no point spending time making a change that accomplishes nothing whatsoever, _and_ breaks compatibility with old versions. It makes no difference if said old versions are well past their due dates.

