Would be nice if there was a `@Decorate` feature. The Decorator Pattern is a great design pattern, however it is sometimes cumbersome to implement for Interfaces with many methods. The following example shows a proposal for the usage of the `@Decorate` feature before and after being Delomboked: 


```java

public interface Vehicle {
    String getA();
    int getB(int n);
    <T> T getC(T t);
    String getD();
    //... and so on
}

public interface Component {
    String getName();
    //... and so on
}

```

**Lombok-ed version**
```java

@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class Car implements Vehicle, Component {
    
    @Decorate(class=Vehicle.class)
    private final Vehicle vehicle;

    @Decorate(class=Component.class)
    private final Component component;

    //User override
    @Override
    public String getD(){
        return "this is a Car calling getD";
    }
}

```

**Delomboked version**

```java

public class Car implements Vehicle {
    private final Vehicle vehicle;
    private final Component component;

    public Car(Vehicle vehicle, Component component){
        this.vehicle = vehicle;
        this.component = component;
    }
    
    //Lombok Override
    @Override
    public String getA(){
        return this.vehicle.getA();
    }

    //Lombok Override
    @Override
    public int getB(int n){
        return this.vehicle.getB(n);
    }

    //Lombok Override
    @Override
    public <T> T getC(T t){
        return this.vehicle.getC(t);
    }

    //User override
    @Override
    public String getD(){
        return "this is a Car calling getD";
    }

    //Lombok override
    @Override
    public String getName(){
        return this.component.getName();
    }
}

```

