```

---

So, when delomboking the class, toBuilder() method differs from the compiled toBuilder() method, which can cause application misbehavior.

Please, fix that.

Thanks,
Al

As a example, let's have these classes:

```
public class Test {
	public static void main(String... args) {
		System.out.println(new A("a"));
		System.out.println(new B("b"));
	}
}
```
```
@ToString
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class A {
	private final String x;

	public String getX() {
		System.out.println("getX() invoked on " + this.getClass());
		return x;
	}
