There are many requests for customizing `@ToString` and other annotations, so I'm proposing a simple way (based on ideas from this [discussion][1]) how many such requests can be easily fullfilled: Allow to exclude fields (already possible) and include methods in the computation. So the solution for #1392 would be simply

```
@ToString
class Article {
    private String author;
    private String title;
    @ToString.Exclude
    private String content;

    @ToString.Include
    private String shortenedContent() {
        return content.substring(0, Math.min(content.length, 100));
    }
}
```

This is surely more verbose than some `@ToString(maxLength=100)`, but imagine you need to append the field length. Or there's another field which should never be shortened. Or another field `signature` which is uninteresting, but you want to see its length. This all can be achieved easily with methods inclusion.

---

An alternative stringly typed syntax: `@ToString(exclude="content", include="shortenedContent()")`.

[1]: https://groups.google.com/d/msg/project-lombok/dc5nXTI3xMU/tkgk0OfbAQAJ

