@omega09 I don't think, it "includes" it, especially it wouldn't allow you to call the Apache builders. But it'd allow you to do about everything their builders can do, except for [styling][], which is an orthogonal feature.

My proposal is good in case you want to change what happens for some fields while leaving lombok do its usual job for the others. Leaving out an offending field has always been possible, but sometimes, that's too harsh. When you want to summarize it instead, my proposal helps. It tries to combine the flexibility of a hand-written method with Lombok's power of handling boilderplate for free.

[styling]: https://commons.apache.org/proper/commons-lang/javadocs/api-3.1/org/apache/commons/lang3/builder/ToStringStyle.html

