`return status == null ? null : status.equals(UserStatus.ACTIVE);`

You want to return `null` if `status` is `null`? That's very unconventional. An `isXXX()` method is accepted as one that returns `true` or `false`. A better implementation would be

    public Boolean isActive() {
        return status == UserStatus.ACTIVE;
    }

which returns `false` is `status` is `null`.

