Ok, despite hours of hacking at it, I stumbled on a simple work around shortly after filing this issue. It'd still be nice to be able to override the toBuilder() method name though. The workaround is you declare the builder class in the superclass, then have the subclass builder class extend it.

```
public static class FooBuilder {
    protected FooBuilder() {} // Required or the subclass can't access the generated private no-arg constructor.
}
public static class FooBarBuilder extends FooBuilder {}
```

