Hello!

Here is a simplified example:
```
@Data
@Builder
@NoArgsConstructor
@AllArgsConstructor
class MyClass {
    @Builder.Default
    private int property = 5;
}

MyClass myObject1 = MyClass.builder().build();
System.out.println(myObject1.getProperty()); // --> 5, OK

MyClass myObject2 = new MyClass();
System.out.println(myObject2.getProperty()); // --> 0, not OK, 5 expected
```

Simple work around if anyone else is having this problem is to set the default values in the inner class instead. 

```@AllArgsConstructor
@Builder
class OuterA {
    @Getter
    // @Default
    private InnerA innerA;
    @Getter
    // @Default
    private InnerB innerB;
    @Getter
    @Singular
    @Default
    private ImmutableList<String> lists = ImmutableList.<String> of();

    static class OuterABuilder {
        private InnerA innerA = InnerA.builder().build();
        private InnerB innerB = InnerB.builder().build();
    }
}
```

