This is not a good idea. Basic semantics: Why would setting the _default_ all of a sudden mean that lombok will call `.addAll` and pass the immutable list it made, instead of just assigning the immutable list it made? This plan will technically result in what you want, but it makes as much sense as saying that you get this behaviour using the `@Banana` annotation. Worse actually, banana at least is a non-sequitur, the text `@Default` would make people think it has something to do with defaults. Surely you see why one would think that. Discoverability and readability of code is very important, and this proposal fails the mark on that so badly, it's not going to happen.

