# Change request
I use Lombok on @Entity annotated classes (i.e. classes used by a JPA ORM framework) and all my entities extend from a base class which adds an ID to the given entity.

As a result I end up with having (/needing) all of the following annotations on my entities:
```java
@Builder
@NoArgsConstructor
@AllArgsConstructor
@Entity
@EqualsAndHashCode(callSuper = true)
@Data
```

This removes a lot of the cool development speed. **I think it would be very nice to have a super annotation**, something a la `@EntityData(withBuilder=true, callSuper=true)`.

## Elaboration
I like to have a builder for each entity. The @Builder annotation creates a constructor with a parameter for each field. But since the entities must have a non-null constructor I end up with the strange mix of @NoArgsConstructor and @AllArgsConstructor (inspired by [this post](https://stackoverflow.com/a/34299054/6095334)).

