From time to time I need to access a data about package/class/interface/field/method reflected information.  
For example:
- Package simple name
- Package fully qualified name
- Class simple name
- Class fully qualified name
- Class implemented interfaces
- Class fields
- Class methods
- Class modifiers
- Field signanture (incl. names, types)
- Field modifiers
- Method signanture (incl. names, types, position)
- Method modifiers
- etc. etc. etc.

This information is easily available at _run-time_.  
But I must have it at *compile-time*.  

Here's where Lombok can come to help.  

In Vanilla Java:  
```Java

package org.example;

import org.apache.commons.lang3.BooleanUtils;

public class system {

	public static String _fqn = "org.example.system";

	public static class feature {

		public static String _fqn = system._fqn + ".feature";

		public static class processor {

			public static String _fqn = feature._fqn + ".processor";

			public static class gpu {

				public static String _fqn = processor._fqn + ".gpu";

				public static final boolean enabled = BooleanUtils.toBoolean(system.feature(_fqn + ".enabled"));

				public static final int threads = NumberUtils.toInt(system.feature(_fqn + ".threads", 1));

				public final String id = "id";

				public final String uid = system.feature(_fqn + ".id");
			}
		}
	}
}
```

With Lombok:  
```Java

package org.example;

import org.apache.commons.lang3.BooleanUtils;

public class system {

	public static class feature {

		public static class processor {

			@Reflector
			public static class gpu {

				@Reflector
				public static final boolean enabled = BooleanUtils.toBoolean(system.feature($reflector.fqn + "." + enabled$reflector.name));

				@Reflector
				public static final int threads = NumberUtils.toInt(system.feature(threads$reflector.fqn, 1));

				@Reflector
				public final String id = id$reflector.name;

				public final String uid = system.feature(id$reflector.fqn);
			}
		}
	}
}

```

Assuming, `system.properties` file:
```Properties
org.example.system.feature.processor.gpu.enabled = true
org.example.system.feature.processor.gpu.threads = 16
```

