I'm aware that you can add annotations to the constructors generated by `@RequiredArgsConstructor`, `@AllArgsConstructor` and `@NoArgsConstructor` by using the `onConstructor_ = {annotation, otherAnnotation}`.

However, what about the parameters of the constructors in `@RequiredArgsConstructor`, `@AllArgsConstructor`? How can I specify them without having to hand-write the constructor?

I digged through the documentation and through the `HandleConstructor.java` file and did not found anything other than `@NonNull` and `@Nullable`. So, I propose something like that:

```java
@AllArgsConstructor(onConstructor_ = @JsonCreator)
public class Foo {
    @ConstructorParam(@JsonProperty("bar"))
    @NonNull
    private String bar;

    @ConstructorParam(@JsonProperty("jog"))
    private @NonNull SomeOtherThing jog;
}
```

The annotation `@ConstructorParam` would be handled by the same handler that handles `@RequiredArgsConstructor` and `@AllArgsConstructor`.

By the way, this could be raised one step further with an hypothetical `@EveryField` annotation:

```java
@AllArgsConstructor(onConstructor_ = @JsonCreator)
@EveryField(onField_ = {
    @NonNull,
    @ConstructorParam(@JsonProperty("{lombok-field-name}"))
})
public class Foo {
    private String bar;
    private SomeOtherThing jog;
}
```

