```java
public class Parent {
    
    String parentField;
    
    @Builder(builderMethodName = "parentBuilder")
    public Parent(String parentField) {
        this.parentField = parentField;
    }
}

public class ChildOne extends Parent {
    
    String childOneField;
    
    @Builder(builderMethodName = "childOneBuilder")
    public ChildOne(String parentField, String childOneField) {
        super(parentField);
        this.childOneField = childOneField;
    }
}

public class ChildTwo extends Parent {

    String childTwoField;
    
    @Builder(builderMethodName = "childTwoBuilder")
    public ChildTwo(String parentField, String childTwoField) {
        super(parentField);
        this.childTwoField = childTwoField;
    }
}
```

# Environment
JDK:        1.8.0U144
Lombok: 1.16.18

# Note
When I use IntelliJ IDEA's _delombok_ function for `@Builder` class-by-class, the project builds and the generated code works very well. If I _delombok_ just one child class - so there will be a child with `@Builder` annotation and one with delomboked build function, the project builds too.

nodes.body:
*@rzwitserloot, please be aware that I did not put the `@Builder` annotation on the child class itself.*

`ChildOneBuilder` doesn't have to know about its parent's field, because I've put the `@Builder` annotation on the child's constructor. `ChildOne`'s constructor has two parameters, so Lombok will generate `ChildOneBuilder`'s code according to this. My example is **working fine if I have just one child**. This **bug appears when I define two children** as you can see the example above.

As I mentioned in the **note** I can delombok one of the child class and Lombok can resolve every parameter.

```
public class ChildTwo extends Parent{
    String childTwoField;

    public ChildTwo(String parentField, String childTwoField) {
        super(parentField);
        this.childTwoField = childTwoField;
    }

    public static ChildTwoBuilder childTwoBuilder() {
        return new ChildTwoBuilder();
    }

    public static class ChildTwoBuilder {
        private String parentField;
        private String childTwoField;

        ChildTwoBuilder() {
        }

        public ChildTwoBuilder parentField(String parentField) {
            this.parentField = parentField;
            return this;
        }

        public ChildTwoBuilder childTwoField(String childTwoField) {
            this.childTwoField = childTwoField;
            return this;
        }

        public ChildTwo build() {
            return new ChildTwo(parentField, childTwoField);
        }

        public String toString() {
            return "ChildTwo.ChildTwoBuilder(parentField=" + this.parentField + ", childTwoField=" + this.childTwoField + ")";
        }
    }
}
```
In this situation (ChildOne uses `@Builder`, ChildTwo has been delomboked) the project is working again.

