@KonradAdamek Things like
```
@Builder(defaultDuration = Duration.ZERO)
@Builder(defaultInstant = Instant.MIN)
...
```
won't compile, unless you add them all to the annotation definition. You'd need a class to instance Map like
```
@Builder.GeneralDefaults
private static final Map<Class<?>, Object> builderDefaults = ImmutableMap.of(
    Duration.class, Duration.ZERO,
    Instant.class = Instant.MIN,
    LocalTime.class, LocalTime.MIN);
```
or maybe just
```
@Builder.GeneralDefaults
private static final Object[] builderDefaults = {Duration.ZERO, Instant.MIN, LocalTime.MIN};
```

I guess, that defaulting to the empty String may be a good idea, but the possibility to default to `"bar"` less so.

For me, repeating `= ""` 25 times would be the way to go as I consider 100 chars to be better than relying on some magic. For a much bigger number, I'd consider defining a Map like above, creating a template instance, filling it via reflection and defining
```
Builder builder() {
    return TEMPLATE_INSTANCE.toBuilder();
}
```

