Having the behaviour as immutable by default is fine, but I completely agree that adding `@Builder.Default` should allow us to specify the collection type in order to allow mutability at our leisure, exactly as @fo0 describes.

At the moment, we have to do this in order to edit the data:
```java
  @Builder
  @Data
  public class Sample {
    @Singular
    private Set<String> labels;
  }
  public class DoSomething {
    public void doSomething() {
      final Sample sample = Sample.builder()
          .label("foo")
          .build();
      doSomethingElse(sample);
    }
    public void doSomethingElse(Sample sample) {
      Set<String> labels = new HashSet<>(sample.getLabels());
      labels.add("bar");
      sample.setLabels(labels);
    }
  }
```
