The new copy field annotations feature copies nullity annotations by default. But it only does so for the first annotation. Problem: there are multiple nullity annotations which have different meaning.

```
@RequiredArgsConstructor
class Test {
    @javax.annotation.Nonnull
    @javax.validation.constraints.NotNull
    final String s1;
}
```

Actual delombok result:
```
    @java.beans.ConstructorProperties({"s1"})
    public Test(@NotNull String s1) {
        this.s1 = s1;
    }
```

Expected:
```
    @java.beans.ConstructorProperties({"s1"})
    public Test(@NotNull @Nonnull String s1) {
        this.s1 = s1;
    }
```

`javax.validation.constraints.NotNull` is used for bean validation. `javax.annotation.Nonnull` is used for static code analysis.

