Using a builder pattern in my opinion is a great way for not having a constructor with a lot of input parameters. It helps code readability big time. To my surprise when the `@Builder` annotation is added on a class a constructor with all the class members is created. Adding `@NoArgsConstructor` will break `@Builder`, too. 

Maybe something like this would be a better approach:

```java
