public Class Foo{
    private int id;
    private String name;

    public Foo setId(final int id){ this.id=id; return this;}
    public Foo setName(final String name){ this.name=name; return this;}

}
```

### Vanilla Java with mutable Foo
```java
try {
    final int assignedId = doStuff(foo) //foo has somehow changed here, maybe an API call or persistence
    return foo.setId(assignedId);
} catch(...){}
```

