**Describe the feature**
You can have multiple lombock annotation in classes. And a lot of time, you always put the sames annotations in each classes depending on the context or the project. The goal of this feature is to allow users to redefine an annotation that merge multiple lombock annotations.  
For instance, if you want to have POJO objects with a builder, today you need to add on all POJOs :
```java
@Getter
@Setter
@NoArgsConstructor
@AllArgsConstructor
@Builder
class MyPojo {}
```
If we have the inheritance on lombock annotation, we would have the ability to create a new one : 
```java
@Getter
@Setter
@NoArgsConstructor
@AllArgsConstructor
@Builder
@Retention(RetentionPolicy.RUNTIME)
@Target(ElementType.TYPE)
public @interface PojoWithBuilder {
}
```
With this, you will only need to add to all your classes the following annotation : 
```java
@PojoWithBuilder
class MyPojo {} 
```

