**Before submitting**
I use a set of lombok's annotations on a web controller dto-s (Value, Builder, etc.) and this automatically adds ToString which is also very useful for logging.
Hovewer, sometimes clients send very large data into some fields (photos in base64). So one field in log can accuire up to 99.99% of the ToString-ed dto.

**Describe the feature**
Add per-field annotation like as ToString.Include or ToString.Exclude to give possibility limit the length of the field. Example:

Before:
```java
@Value
public class SomeDto {
    
    String filename;
    
    LocalDateTime created;
    
    String mimeType;
    
    // Really big string, kb or even mb!
    String contentsBase64;
}
...
log.info("Dto: {}", dto); // Messy uncopyable output.
```
After:
```java
@Value
public class SomeDto {
    
    String filename;
    
    LocalDateTime created;
    
    String mimeType;
    
    @ToString.LimitLength(16)
    String contentsBase64;
}
...
