I believe you're hitting a racing condition bug @burdoto; the worst kind of bug. The constructor generated for CodeBottle will first set instance variable `lazyLoading` and then set `token` and `httpClient`. That's pretty consistent with vanilla java when you mix setting the field at the declaration and setting fields in the constructor. But, in your case, setting `lazyLoading` means starting two new threads that will be accessing field `httpClient`. If the threads access `httpClient` before the constructor can finished running, you will get a null pointer. 

I ran a sample test with a custom constructor that waits to create the lazyLoading threads until after httpClient is set and the NullPointerException goes away. I would offer that this is not a bug in Lombok.

``` java
    private final @Nullable String token;
    private @Getter final OkHttpClient httpClient;
    public final CompletableFuture<Void> lazyLoading;
    
    public CodeBottle() {
        token = null;
        httpClient = new OkHttpClient.Builder().build();
    	lazyLoading = CompletableFuture.allOf(requestLanguages(), requestCategories());
    }
```

