The basic concept is to create an inner class that holds all fields you don't want exposed to the builder.

- Define inner class with private unexposed fields.
- Create a final instance field of the inner class type in the root class and initialize it in the declaration.
    - This prevents any setters from being generated as well as causes it to be excluded from the Builder.
    - This also prevents the field from appearing in the constructor generated by '@AllArgsConstructor'
