I use static imports quite a lot for frequently used methods. Was quite surprised code which worked fine in eclipse failed to compile in a maven build. Basically maven compiler could not find any lombok generated code.

Narrowed down the problem to the @UtilityClass which automatically converts  **public instance**  methods to **public static** methods. 

Lets consider the following example:
```
import lombok.experimental.UtilityClass;
/**
 */
@UtilityClass
public class Utility {

  /**
   */
  public void utilityMethod() {
    System.out.print("Instance method made static");
  }
}
```
```
import static x.test.Utility.utilityMethod;

/**
 */
public class Main {

  /**
   * @param args
   */
  public static void main(String[] args) {
    utilityMethod();
  }

}
```

When I run the code from eclipse everything works fine.
However when I do a maven clean install I get the following error:
```
[ERROR] Failed to execute goal org.apache.maven.plugins:maven-compiler-plugin:3.1:compile (default-compile) on project x: Compilation failure: Compilation failure:
[ERROR] /C:/JavaDev/Workspaces/x/src/main/java/x/test/Main.java:[8,1] cannot find symbol
[ERROR]   symbol:   static utilityMethod
[ERROR]   location: class
[ERROR] /C:/JavaDev/Workspaces/x/src/main/java/x/test/Main.java:[18,5] cannot find symbol
[ERROR]   symbol:   method utilityMethod()
[ERROR]   location: class x.test.Main
```

The fix to the problem is quite simple just explicitly specify in the utility class that the method is static. However it`s quite easy to make such an error since as far as the IDE is concerned the method is static.

