@IDVsbruck Yeah, I think we can shortcut this issue down to: Actually, lombok ought to be making it static at which point the 1 param issue becomes irrelevant.

The one downside is that you can't put static classes inside non-static classes, but, how often are people gonna try that one? It'd have to look like:

```java
class Outer {
    class AnInnerClassThatIsNotStatic {
        @UtilityClass /* uh oh */
        class Helper {}
    }
}
```

In that case we should probably just error out and go: You just can't put utility classes in this location, it makes no sense to have a non-static one in the first place, and there's nothing lombok can do here to make it static. Besides, we can't make any elements inside this thing static either.

So, sounds like we should:

* Add 'static' if it isn't there and the annotated class is a class (and not an interface or enum or whatnot), and its enclosing type is a class (and not an interface or enum or whatnot). This is technically backwards incompatible, but given that it's [A] weird and [B] already doesn't work, I don't think it matters.
* Before adding static, check if the parent class is itself 'non-static' (which requires checking if it has a static modifier, and if it does not, if has an enclosing type and if it does, if that is a class and not an interface, enum, record, etc) – and then do absolutely no modifying of any code and generate an error message instead on that node.

