It would be useful to generate checkerframework's `@Pure` annotation at least for generated getters and setters. See example below:

    // example field with generated getter
    @Getter
    private @Nullable String field;

This assumes we have  configured lombok with `lombok.addNullAnnotations = checkerframework`.
Now, without `@Pure` the following statement makes checkerframework raise the error: `error: [dereference.of.nullable] dereference of possibly-null reference getField()`.

    System.err.println(getField() == null ? "" : getField().toString());

Adding `@Pure` to `getField()` will not raise the error for the second occurence of `getField()` since checkerframework will know calling `getField()` does not change state.

