@ExtensionMethod is so close to MVP as just a Fluent Interface to static method transformation system

**Describe the bug**
When chaining several methods together, it is common to call a real method at the end.  Lombok appears to be attempting to convert the real method to a static call.  It should only convert calls to static methods that exist in the "extension classes"

**To Reproduce**
1  Create a static "extension" method:
public static <T> List<T> toList(Iterator<T> collection) {
  List<T> result  = new ArrayList<T>();
  collection.forEachReamaining(result::add);
  return result;
}

2  Create a static "extension" method:
public static <T> Iterator<T> method1(Iterator<T> collection) { return collection; }

3 Write a calling sequence such as:
List<String> list = new Arrays.asList({"Joe", "Fred", "John", "Mary");
list.iterator().method1().toList().forEach(System.out::println);

