**Workarkounds**
1. Use another name for the builder method by setting it via the parameter "builderMethodName". This would have to be done for each inheritance layer that has to affected generic typing. The downside of this approach is, we're polluting our class with builder methods.
```java
@SuperBuilder(builderMethodName = "baseBuilder")
public class ClassA<T> { }
```
```java
@SuperBuilder
public class ClassB<T> extends ClassA<Optional<T>> { }
```

2. Drop fixed types by overriding the builder method by using a wildcard. The downside of this approach is, that we're out of the type-safe world from here on.
```java
@SuperBuilder
public class ClassA<T> {
    public static <T> ClassABuilder<?, ?, ?> builder() {
        return new ClassABuilderImpl<T>();
    }
}
```

Can confirm, but I haven't found a way to fix this. It may well be that this case is beyond the limits of Java generics.

Maybe someone else finds a (type-safe) way to make this code compile (this is what lombok generates at the moment):

```
public class ClassA<S> {
	public static abstract class ClassABuilder<S, C extends ClassA<S>, B extends ClassA.ClassABuilder<S, C, B>> {
		protected abstract B self();
		public abstract C build();
	}

	private static final class ClassABuilderImpl<S> extends
			ClassA.ClassABuilder<S, ClassA<S>, ClassA.ClassABuilderImpl<S>> {
		@java.lang.Override
		protected ClassA.ClassABuilderImpl<S> self() {
			return this;
		}

		@java.lang.Override
		public ClassA<S> build() {
			return new ClassA<S>(this);
		}
	}

	protected ClassA(final ClassA.ClassABuilder<S, ?, ?> b) {
	}

	public static <S> ClassA.ClassABuilder<S, ?, ?> builder() {
		return new ClassA.ClassABuilderImpl<S>();
	}
}

public class ClassB<T> extends ClassA<java.util.Optional<T>> {
	public static abstract class ClassBBuilder<T, C extends ClassB<T>, B extends ClassB.ClassBBuilder<T, C, B>>
			extends ClassA.ClassABuilder<java.util.Optional<T>, C, B> {
		@java.lang.Override
		protected abstract B self();
		@java.lang.Override
		public abstract C build();
	}

	private static final class ClassBBuilderImpl<T> extends
			ClassB.ClassBBuilder<T, ClassB<T>, ClassB.ClassBBuilderImpl<T>> {
		@java.lang.Override
		protected ClassB.ClassBBuilderImpl<T> self() {
			return this;
		}

		@java.lang.Override
		public ClassB<T> build() {
			return new ClassB<T>(this);
		}
	}

	protected ClassB(final ClassB.ClassBBuilder<T, ?, ?> b) {
		super(b);
	}

	public static <T> ClassB.ClassBBuilder<T, ?, ?> builder() {
		return new ClassB.ClassBBuilderImpl<T>();
	}
}
```

