**Describe the bug**

Hi. `lombok.NonNull` is handled differently from checkerframework.NonNull. lomboks `@NonNull` works on Constructors and method parameters. Checkerframeworks `@NonNull` only works on constructors.

**To Reproduce**

Given this class:

```java
import lombok.Value;
import org.checkerframework.checker.nullness.qual.NonNull;

@Value
class Test {
    @lombok.NonNull String lombokNonNull;
    @NonNull String checkerNonNull;

    public void lombokNonNull(@lombok.NonNull String foo) {
        System.out.println(foo);
    }

    public void checkerNonNull(@NonNull String foo) {
        System.out.println(foo);
    }
}
```

This

```java
new Test(null, "non-null");
```

fails with a NPE, expected and great. (testing lomboks `@NonNull` on ctor)

This

```java
new Test("non-null", null);
```

also fails with a NPE, which proves that lombok has some handling of checkerframeworks `@NonNull`. (testing checkerframeworks `@NonNull` on ctor)

this:

```java
new Test("", "").lombokNonNull(null);
```

fails with a NPE, expected and great. (testing lomboks `@NonNull` on methods)

But:

```java
new Test("", "").checkerNonNull(null);
```

doesn't fail with a NPE. (testing checkerframeworks `@NonNull` on methods)

**Expected behavior**

I would expect that checkerframeworks `@NonNull` either works on the constructor and on the method or it doesn't work in either case. That it works on constructor but not on methods is strange.

It would be great if the checkerframework `@NonNull` is applicable everywhere where lomboks `@NonNull` works.

