Description:
Provide a mechanism to have a constructor generated by `@Builder`  to accept an instance of the builder, rather than an all-args constructor.  This prevents objects from ever being created by calling constructors directly. I believe using auto generated constructors can be dangerous. Changing the order that fields are declared within a class becomes a breaking change.

Here's a sample of a POJO, and how it is delomoked today:
Before Delombok:
```java
@Builder
public class SomePojo {
  
    private final String firstName;
    private final String lastName;
    
}
```

```java
public class SomePojo {
  
    private final String firstName;
    private final String lastName;

    SomePojo(String firstName, String lastName) {
        this.firstName = firstName;
        this.lastName = lastName;
    }

    public static SomePojoBuilder builder() {
        return new SomePojoBuilder();
    }

    public static class SomePojoBuilder {
        private String firstName;
        private String lastName;

        SomePojoBuilder() {
        }

        public SomePojoBuilder firstName(String firstName) {
            this.firstName = firstName;
