A simple refactoring which may seemingly be non-breaking, but actually be breaking:
```java
@Builder
public class SomePojo {

    private final String lastName;
    private final String firstName;
    

}
```

Now delomboked:
```java
public class SomePojo {

    private final String lastName;
    private final String firstName;

    SomePojo(String lastName, String firstName) {
        this.lastName = lastName;
        this.firstName = firstName;
    }

    public static SomePojoBuilder builder() {
        return new SomePojoBuilder();
    }


    public static class SomePojoBuilder {
        private String lastName;
        private String firstName;

        SomePojoBuilder() {
        }

        public SomePojoBuilder lastName(String lastName) {
            this.lastName = lastName;
            return this;
        }

        public SomePojoBuilder firstName(String firstName) {
            this.firstName = firstName;
            return this;
        }

        public SomePojo build() {
            return new SomePojo(lastName, firstName);
        }

        public String toString() {
            return "SomePojo.SomePojoBuilder(lastName=" + this.lastName + ", firstName=" + this.firstName + ")";
        }
    }
}
```

This isn't a problem for any code creating SomePojo with `SomePojo.builder().firstName("first").lastName("last")`, but could go undetected if any code is calling `new SomePojo("first","last")`.

I think the generated code would be safer if switched to generate a Pojo like:
```java
public class SomePojo {

    private final String lastName;
    private final String firstName;

    private SomePojo(SomePojoBuilder builder) {
        this.lastName = builder.lastName;
        this.firstName = builder.firstName;
    }

    public static SomePojoBuilder builder() {
        return new SomePojoBuilder();
    }


    public static class SomePojoBuilder {
        private String lastName;
        private String firstName;

        private SomePojoBuilder() {
        }

        public SomePojoBuilder lastName(String lastName) {
            this.lastName = lastName;
            return this;
        }

        public SomePojoBuilder firstName(String firstName) {
            this.firstName = firstName;
            return this;
        }

        public SomePojo build() {
            return new SomePojo(this);
        }

        public String toString() {
            return "SomePojo.SomePojoBuilder(lastName=" + this.lastName + ", firstName=" + this.firstName + ")";
        }
    }
}
```

This would be a potentially breaking change. This may be a candidate for a lombok config flag.

