**Describe the bug**
Given a Class with a @ Builder(toBuilder = true) and a field List<> marked as @ Singular then the setter of the builder given by toBuilder() method merges the passed list to the one previously existing instead of using it as the new list.

**To Reproduce**
```
@Builder(toBuilder = true)
@Getter
public class Example {
    @Singular
    private final List<String> foos;

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Example example1 = Example.builder()
                .foos(Arrays.asList("1", "2"))
                .build();
        
        Example modifiedExample1 = example1.toBuilder()
                .foos(Collections.singletonList("3"))
                .build();
        
        System.out.println(modifiedExample1.getFoos()); //prints [1, 2, 3]    
    }
}
```

**Expected behavior**
I understand that the purpose of @ Singular is to add a singular method  _foo()_ to add items one by one, and there the expectation is that they are all added to the list, that's OK, but why modify the behavior of the plural function _foos()_ ?
One would think that the behavior of the builder's _foos()_ would be the same as when the @ Singular annotation is not present.

**Version info (please complete the following information):**
 - Lombok version 1.18.12 
 - Platform javac 11.0.8 (AdoptOpenJDK) Intellij Idea 2020.1.1

I apology in advance for my English, I am not a native speaker.

**Describe the bug**

In Lombok 1.18.10, a method used for `@Builder.ObtainVia` can return a different type than the one declared for the field, as long as there is builder method accepting the relevant type. This is no longer supported in Lombok 1.18.12 due to a refactorization of the generated code. This was useful for example for value types with private nullable fields with a non-nullable `Optional` getter.


**To Reproduce**

Minimal example:

```
package org.example;

import java.util.Optional;
import lombok.Builder;
import lombok.NonNull;

@Builder(toBuilder = true)
public class LombokObtainViaOtherType {

  @Builder.ObtainVia(method = "getFoo")
  private final String foo;

  public Optional<String> getFoo() {
    return Optional.ofNullable(foo);
  }

  public static class LombokObtainViaOtherTypeBuilder {
    LombokObtainViaOtherTypeBuilder foo(@NonNull Optional<String> foo) {
      this.foo = foo.orElse(null);
      return this;
    }
  }
}
```

In Lombok 1.18.12 and later, this code fails with the error:

```
LombokObtainViaOtherType.java:5: error: incompatible types: Optional<String> cannot be converted to String
```

Delombok shows why. Lombok 1.18.10 produces:

```
  @java.lang.SuppressWarnings("all")
  @lombok.Generated
  public LombokObtainViaOtherTypeBuilder toBuilder() {
    return new LombokObtainViaOtherTypeBuilder().foo(this.getFoo());
  }
```

while Lombok 1.18.12 produces:

```
  @java.lang.SuppressWarnings("all")
  @lombok.Generated
  public LombokObtainViaOtherType.LombokObtainViaOtherTypeBuilder toBuilder() {
    final String foo = this.getFoo();
    return new LombokObtainViaOtherType.LombokObtainViaOtherTypeBuilder().foo(foo);
  }
```

So Lombok 1.18.12 and later assumes that the `@Builder.ObtainVia` method returns the field's declared type, while Lombok 1.18.10 and earlier only assume that there exists _some_ builder method that accepts the returned type.


**Expected behavior**
I expected my code to keep working after a Lombok upgrade, but perhaps this is an unintended "feature" that only worked by accident. Either way I figured I'd report it since the change broke some code, but I half-expect this is a wontfix.

**Version info (please complete the following information):**
 - Lombok version: 1.18.12 or later
 - Platform: javac 11.0.8

**Additional context**

The real-world example that exposed this was, among other similar cases in the same project, [this `timeout` member](https://github.com/Yubico/java-webauthn-server/commit/871c4e2fde9d38194781c9f039a7214cb00511fe#diff-82e188a36bf80f4249d49274a8e1427d0d53ca2bd762d383579a2ff08cd1b4ccR66-R67) and [its associated builder method](https://github.com/Yubico/java-webauthn-server/commit/871c4e2fde9d38194781c9f039a7214cb00511fe#diff-82e188a36bf80f4249d49274a8e1427d0d53ca2bd762d383579a2ff08cd1b4ccR154-R157).

