It's a well know practice to map enums to key values and search them via a static .findByField method, most of the time the method is just a iteration in values() and a match return of the field, we can also implement it via a Map and lazy cache it. I propose a @IndexedEnumField ~(the name is whatever, we can bikeshed it)~ annotation for introducing a well implemented .findByField static method for each field or getter it's annottated. I found this pattern in a lot of large projects and most don't benefit from HashMaps or are repeated in all enums for all fields that are needed. For cases that a Map is not useful (same field for more than 1 enum instance, and other cases) the user is not recommended to use this annotation.

Pluses:
- In the case the .findByMethod method is already implemented we can just provide a static Map in the form INDEXED_FIELD for providing a easy way of normalization before finding
- Option to not generate a method and instead just create a static map with the values, again for providing custom normalization
- Return Optional instead of null when not found
- Visibility and modifiers control of the static method
- Option to choose the map implementation (TreeMap, EnumMap, third party implementations, etc)

Edit: Assumedly being naive here, I think it's maybe not that difficult given most of the transformations are already being used in other annotations and might try a stab at the implementation if we have a good feeback

Lomboked version:
``` java
public enum DayOfWeek {
    SUN(1, "Sunday"),
    MON(2, "Monday"),
    TUE(3, "Tuesday"),
    WED(4, "Wednesday"),
    THU(5, "Thursday"),
    FRI(6, "Friday"),
    SAT(7, "Saturday"),
    ;

    @IndexedEnumField
    private final int calendarDay;

    private final String fullName;

    DayOfWeek(int calendarDay, String fullName) {
        this.calendarDay = calendarDay;
        this.fullName = fullName;
        EnumMap
    }

    // Custom internal getter for normalizing before indexing
    @IndexedEnumField
    private String getLowerCaseFullName() {
        return fullName.toLowerCase();
    }

    // Custom findBy for normalizing the search term to lowercase
    static Optional<DayOfWeek> findByFullName(String searchingName) {
        if (searchingName == null) return Optional.empty();
        return Optional.ofNullable(INDEXED_LOWER_CASE_FULL_NAME.get(searchingName.toLowerCase()));
    }

}
```

