**Describe the feature**
A boolean toggle setter, that generates a function that, when called, flips the boolean's state. This can be done either with a field on the `@Setter` (maybe `@Setter(generateInverter = true)`), or with a separate  annotation extending `Setter`. 

### Lomboked Code:
```java
public class Main {

	@lombok.Setter
	@lombok.Getter
	@Lombok.Inverter
	private boolean test;

	public static void main(final String[] args) {

	}
}
```

### Or, alternatively
```java
public class Main {

	@lombok.Setter
	@lombok.Getter(generateInverter = true)
	private boolean test;

	public static void main(final String[] args) {

	}
}
```

### Delomboked Code:
```java
public class Main {

	private boolean test;

	public static void main(final String[] args) {

	}

	public boolean isTest() {
		return test;
	}

	public void setTest(final boolean $test) {
		test = $test;
	}

	public void setTest() {
		test = !test;
	}

}
```

**Describe the target audience**
This would be useful for setting flags. Especially if you are only going to set the flag once, and you know the predefined value, calling the inverter function is a bit cleaner. Obviously it is also useful if you want to flip the value of the boolean, as instead of doing `main.setTest(!main.getTest())` you can just do `main.setTest()`. Perhaps the overloaded `setTest` may not be the best name, I am open to ideas for other names (perhaps `flipTest` or allowing you to customize the name?).

**Additional context**
None.

