I think my example with `Animal` and `Cat` only worked because they were in the same package. Moving `Cat` to a different package results in compilation failure.
I think one way to solve it would be to tell lombok explicitly about sub-types and super-type for visitor generation with the annotation itself. For example:
```java
@Visitor(child = {Cat.class})
public interface Animal {
}
```

```java
@Visitable(for = Animal.class)
public class Cat implements Animal {
}
