Currently when we use the combination 

```
@Builder
@AllArgsConstructor
```
we can save a lot of code. However, there is currently no hook to put, e.g. a validation routine for the built instance, thus we must explicitly create constructors or static methods  annotated with `@Builder` if we need such a validation routing for only a few of those built properties.

**Describe the feature**
`@Builder(afterBuiltMethodName="methodName")` hooks into the building step by executing the method after the instance was built by the builder.

**Example:**

```
@Builder(afterBuiltMethodName="validateInstance")
@AllArgsConstructor
class User {

    private final Integer id;

    // a lot of other properties ..

    void validateInstance() {
        Objects.requireNonNull(this.id, "Id must not be null");
    }
}
```

