I want to use `@With` Lombok on my JPA entities and can't have them making new instances of themselves. Therefore, I propose adding a boolean attribute to `@With` that controls if a new object is returned or the current instance is mutated. 

Per [@With documentation](https://projectlombok.org/features/With) Lombok generates the method
```
  public WithExample withName(String name) {
    return this.name == name ? this : new WithExample(name, age);
  }
```

whereas `@With(clone=false)` would generate
```
  public WithExample withName(String name) {
    this.name = name;
    return this;
  }
```

The default of the new attribute should be the current behavior so that this is 100% backwards compatible.

