Sorry, I didn't think about that as I've been using them for quite a while as preview features. I've seen that the PR has been merged, but I've found a bug. First of all, it's important to remember that records cannot extend classes, but they can implement interfaces. When using delombok on a record annotated with a Lombok annotation that implements an interface the record header is shifted after the implements clause which is syntactically wrong.

Input:
