**Describe the bug**
The vanilla Java of the lazy getter has a code smell.
https://www.projectlombok.org/features/GetterLazy

The AtomicReference variable is used to cache the calculated result. If that outcome is null, the pointer of the AtomicReference is set in the AtomicReference!?! Having AtomicReference contain something is indeed needed to prevent recalculation of the outcome, but this solution misuses the variable to contain something that was not intended (based on the variable name), adds a cyclic reference and adds the need of casting an Object to the actual type.

Developers may use online Java code snippets as an example/inspiration, also this vanilla Java code snippet. Snippets should be free of code smells (given some code smells are subjective), unless it is there to demonstrate a code smell.

