**Describe the feature**
Would it be possible to generate an empty Example.validateBuilder(ExampleBuilder) or ExampleBuilder.validate() method?  This method would be called at the start of ExampleBuilder.build() to sanitize data or throw exceptions in order to prevent the object from being constructed with an invalid state.  For example:

```java
@Builder
@Value
class Person {
    String name;
    ...

    class PersonBuilder {
        @Override
        private void validate() {
            if (name == null || name.isBlank()) {
                throw new IllegalStateException("name is required");
            } 
        }
    }
}
```
or
```java
@Builder
@Value
class SearchRequest {
    String indexName;
    int page;
    ...

    @Override
    private void validateBuilder(SearchRequestBuilder b) {
        if (b.indexName() == null || b.indexName().isBlank()) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("indexName is required");
        } 
        if (b.page() <= 0) {
            b.page(1);
        } 
    }
}
```

**Describe the target audience**
E for Everyone.  Anyone who uses `@Builder` frequently and would like to be able to prevent invalid configurations from generating an instance.

