Hi! In case this is still relevant for you: Builder creates a private all-args constructor. So if you want to add any logic (like fallbacks for bad values, etc.), you should just add an explicit constructor for lombok.

For your example to work as expected, the code would look like this:

```java
public class Foo {
    private Integer value;
    private Boolean even;

    @Builder
    public Foo(Integer value) {
        this.value = value;
        this.even = (value & 1) == 0;
    }

    // ... getters and optional setters if needed
}
```

This solution also works with `final` fields, since they are set correctly in a constructor. In addition, your class can also have constructors that are not used by the builder.

Imho the current solution works perfectly fine and using setters instead would be an inferior solution.

