@filiphr fantastic breakdown, thanks!

Yes, this sounds like a chicken-and-egg issue, where lombok just can't "get there fast enough", and javac just locks in that said variable isn't there at the time it needs to be there. The 'rounds' system perhaps isn't up to the job of leaving certain annotations unmentioned and in limbo because they may themselves be generated in another round (as they can't be 'completed' yet, due to missing constant values, as lombok hasn't generated the field name constants yet).

Thus, fixing this would be incredibly difficult / requires a re-design of how lombok works at its core, which may happen someday but for different reasons than this issue. Thus, I think it's best we just close it, unless I'm missing something or someone else wants to invest some time and do more research, in case it's not as dire as I think it is?

Thanks for your persistence @anno1985. It made me look into it again.

In Java there is a difference what the compiler does for a single `@Mapping` and multiple repeatable `@Mapping`. When there are multiple repeatable `@Mapping` the compiler first tries to wrap them in the repeatable `@Mappings`. I am not sure when this happens, but I guess this is one of the first things that the compiler does before invoking the annotation processors.

Long story short when I replace

```
@Mapping(target = Entity.Fields.propertyWithoutCounterpart, ignore = true)
@Mapping(target = Entity.Fields.entityProperty, source = "dtoProperty")
```

with

```
@Mappings({
    @Mapping(target = Entity.Fields.propertyWithoutCounterpart, ignore = true),
    @Mapping(target = Entity.Fields.entityProperty, source = "dtoProperty")
})
```

then everything works correctly. I believe that this is the case since the compiler does not need to perform the wrapping at this point since it is already done.

@rzwitserloot I think that you can close this issue. It is a chicken-and-egg issue, but it seems like there is a workaround around that issue as well, by the user doing some of the work of the compiler 😄

