**Describe the bug**
I know if we put a `lombok.NonNull` on a field. Then lombok `RequiredArgsConstructor` helps generate a constructor with a null-check statement. However, if I replace `lombok.NonNull` with `org.springframework.lang.NonNull`, it could still generate a null-check statement. Does `RequiredArgsConstructor` recognize other packages' `NonNull`? Is this expected?

Source:
```
import lombok.RequiredArgsConstructor;
import org.springframework.lang.NonNull;

@RequiredArgsConstructor
public
class MyTest {
  @NonNull private String username;
}
```

Generated:
```
import lombok.RequiredArgsConstructor;
import org.springframework.lang.NonNull;

@RequiredArgsConstructor
public
class MyTest {
  @NonNull String field;

  public MyTest(@NonNull final String username) {
      if (username == null) {
        throw new NullPointerException("username is marked non-null but is null");
      }
      this.username = username;
  }
}
```

**Describe the bug**
When using `@Builder` on a class with Jackson annotations, all annotations are copied correctly except `com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.annotation.JsonTypeIdResolver`.



**To Reproduce**
A runnable demonstration can be found here: https://github.com/Nithanim/lombok-jackson-builder-bug/blob/master/src/main/java/test/ItemInfo.java (Has main class and a JUnit test that calls it, so `mvn test` works.)

A slightly cut-down version you can find below, runnable with Jackson Databind and lombok on the classpath: 
```java
@Value
@Builder
public class ItemInfo {
  @JsonTypeInfo(
      use = JsonTypeInfo.Id.CUSTOM,
      include = JsonTypeInfo.As.EXTERNAL_PROPERTY,
      property = "type",
      visible = true)
  @JsonTypeIdResolver(ItemTypeResolver.class)
  String details;

  public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
    Field field = ItemInfo.class.getDeclaredField("details");
    Objects.requireNonNull(field.getAnnotation(JsonTypeInfo.class));
    Objects.requireNonNull(field.getAnnotation(JsonTypeIdResolver.class));

    Method method = ItemInfo.ItemInfoBuilder.class.getMethod("details", String.class);
    Objects.requireNonNull(method.getAnnotation(JsonTypeInfo.class), "JsonTypeInfo not on builder");
    // This fails
    Objects.requireNonNull(
        method.getAnnotation(JsonTypeIdResolver.class), "JsonTypeIdResolver not on builder");
  }

  public static class ItemTypeResolver extends TypeIdResolverBase {
    @Override
    public String idFromValue(Object o) {
      return null;
    }
    @Override
    public String idFromValueAndType(Object o, Class<?> aClass) {
      return null;
    }
    @Override
    public JsonTypeInfo.Id getMechanism() {
      return null;
    }
  }
}
```

**Expected behavior**
The `com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.annotation.JsonTypeIdResolver` is copied from the field to the builder method like other Jackson annotations.

Executing the test above no longer fails and the setter method in the generated builder class file is annotated with the same `JsonTypeIdResolver` as the field.

