is fucking stupid. You may quote me. Given that it is so incredibly obvious that the above is just so, so, so stupid, the fact that many linter tools nevertheless require you to do the above is irrelevant. We'll go real far in catering to common standards and tools, but there are limits to everything. This is the limit for us - if lombok's javadoc-setter behaviour is making your linters trigger, fix your linter or file bugs with them. We're not 'fixing' this.

For 'setters' in builders, we add exactly that which isn't quite entirely obvious, though it's close. (The fact that the builder's `name()` method returns itself is extremely arguably non-obvious; it certainly isn't inherently encased in the name of the method itself – though the name of the type, i.e. `PersonBuilder`, almost implies it).  Hence, we add that part.

