**Describe the feature**
Allows specifying method names and numbers generated by ```@Setter``` and ```@Getter```.  
``` Java
// Lombok code example:
@Data
public class IssuerIdentificationNumber {

    // The @Setter and @Getter here will override the strategy of the @Data
    @Setter(methodNames = {"setMII", "setMajorIndustryIdentifier"})
    @Getter({"getMII", "getMajorIndustryIdentifier"})
    private MajorIndustryIdentifier mii;

    private CountryCode countryCode;

    private IssuerIdentifier issuerId;

}
```
``` Java
// The final code:
public class IssuerIdentificationNumber {

    private MajorIndustryIdentifier mii;

    private CountryCode countryCode;

    private IssuerIdentifier issuerId;

    // No setMii method
    public void setMII(MajorIndustryIdentifier mii) {
        this.mii = mii;
    }

    // Alias of method setMII
    public void setMajorIndustryIdentifier(MajorIndustryIdentifier mii) {
        this.mii = mii;
    }

    // No getMii method
    public MajorIndustryIdentifier getMII() {
        return mii;
    }

    // Alias of method getMII
    public MajorIndustryIdentifier getMajorIndustryIdentifier() {
        return mii;
    }

    // omit more code
    ......

}
```

**Describe the target audience**
Sometimes Lombok doesn't handle abbreviated words well, like ```url``` or ```mii``` in this issue. Hopefully Lombok can allow to participate in method generation to help it use the better name. And, when an alias method is required, if Lombok could do more, I would no longer have to manually write one method to call another, cleaner code and less work would be great.

