**Describe the feature**
Well, I use Spring Framework for my every-day work and very often use `@RequiredArgsConstructor(or @AllArgsConstrcutor)` for bean creation. And typical service looks like this:

```
@Service
@RequiredArgsConstructor
class SomeService {
    
    private final DependencyBeanOne one;
    private final DependencyBeanTwo two;
    
    //... some methods
}
```

Imagine the situation, when we have several beans of DependencyBeanTwo type. Then we needda get rid of perfect lombok annotation and use plain constructor declaration to set `@Qualifier` annotation:

```
@Service
class SomeService {

    private final DependencyBeanOne one;
    private final DependencyBeanTwo two;

    public SomeService(
        DependencyBeanOne one,
        @Qualifier("theNeededOne")
        DependencyBeanTwo two
    ) {
        this.one = one;
        this.two = two;
    }
//... some methods
}
```
Or another case: using `@Lazy` annotation for injecting bean lazily. 
Sometimes number of dependencies reaches 10+ and such constructor looks owful.

Main proposal: could you, please implement `@RequiredArgsConstructor` annotation to generate constructor, which would take in account all the annotations placed upon fields and give us an opportunity to  replace the last block of code by the following one:
```
@Service
@RequiredArgsConstructor
class SomeService {

    private final DependencyBeanOne one;
    @Qualifier("theNeededOne")
    private final DependencyBeanTwo two;

//... some methods
}
```

From my point of view, it would be a perfect enhancement.

