@rzwitserloot There is a link in my post
https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/21/core/virtual-threads.html
where they explain the problem with ```synchronized``` and thread "pinning"
There are also many amazing videos on youtube about this subject.

TL;DR: JDK 21 Virtual Threads don’t like synchronized, and JDK dev team recommends ReentrantLock instead.

```@Lock``` (or similar) must be almost the same as ```@Synchronized```, but the hidden lock field must be ReenterantLock instead of Object[]

```java
hiddenField.lock();
try {
Body of the method
} finally {
hiddenField.unlock();
}
```

To make it perfect, you can probably add boolean option ```lockInterruptibly``` to this annotation: to call lockInterruptibly() instead of lock(). By default it must be false i.e. ```lock()```

