**Describe the bug**
When annotating a class implementing an interface, the generated equals breaks the symmetry contract [defined in the javadoc](https://docs.oracle.com/javase%2F7%2Fdocs%2Fapi%2F%2F/java/lang/Object.html#equals(java.lang.Object)):

>  The equals method implements an equivalence relation on non-null object references:
> 
>  - It is reflexive: for any non-null reference value x, x.equals(x) should return true.
>  - **It is symmetric: for any non-null reference values x and y, x.equals(y) should return true if and only if y.equals(x) returns true.**
>  -  It is transitive: for any non-null reference values x, y, and z, if x.equals(y) returns true and y.equals(z) returns true, then x.equals(z) should return true.
>  -  It is consistent: for any non-null reference values x and y, multiple invocations of x.equals(y) consistently return true or consistently return false, provided no information used in equals comparisons on the objects is modified.
>  -  For any non-null reference value x, x.equals(null) should return false. 

**To Reproduce**
A simple implementation of Set:
```java
package com.bioserenity.smartwearables.platform.security.model.authorization;

import lombok.EqualsAndHashCode;

import java.util.Collection;
import java.util.HashSet;
import java.util.Iterator;
import java.util.Set;

@EqualsAndHashCode
public class FooSet implements Set<Integer> {

    private final Set<Integer> innerSet;

    public FooSet() {
        this.innerSet = new HashSet<>();
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Set<Integer> hashSet = new HashSet<>();
        FooSet fooSet = new FooSet();

        hashSet.add(1);
        fooSet.add(1);

        System.out.println("HashSet.equals(FooSet) : " + hashSet.equals(fooSet)); // prints true
        System.out.println("FooSet.equals(HashSet) : " + fooSet.equals(hashSet)); // prints false
    }

    @Override
    public int size() {
        return this.innerSet.size();
    }

    @Override
    public boolean isEmpty() {
        return this.innerSet.isEmpty();
    }

    @Override
    public boolean contains(Object o) {
        return this.innerSet.contains(o);
    }

    @Override
    public Iterator<Integer> iterator() {
        return this.innerSet.iterator();
    }

    @Override
    public Object[] toArray() {
        return this.innerSet.toArray();
    }

    @Override
    public <T> T[] toArray(T[] a) {
        return this.innerSet.toArray(a);
    }

    @Override
    public boolean add(Integer integer) {
        return this.innerSet.add(integer);
    }

    @Override
    public boolean remove(Object o) {
        return this.innerSet.remove(o);
    }

    @Override
    public boolean containsAll(Collection<?> c) {
        return this.innerSet.containsAll(c);
    }

    @Override
    public boolean addAll(Collection<? extends Integer> c) {
        return this.innerSet.addAll(c);
    }

    @Override
    public boolean retainAll(Collection<?> c) {
        return this.innerSet.retainAll(c);
    }

    @Override
    public boolean removeAll(Collection<?> c) {
        return this.innerSet.removeAll(c);
    }

    @Override
    public void clear() {
        this.innerSet.clear();
    }
}
```

When delomboking the annotation we can see that the equals tries to check if the other object is `instanceof FooSet` instead of `Set`, and returns false otherwise : 

```java
    public boolean equals(final Object o) {
        if (o == this) return true;
        if (!(o instanceof FooSet)) return false;
        final FooSet other = (FooSet) o;
        if (!other.canEqual((Object) this)) return false;
        final Object this$innerSet = this.innerSet;
        final Object other$innerSet = other.innerSet;
        if (this$innerSet == null ? other$innerSet != null : !this$innerSet.equals(other$innerSet)) return false;
        return true;
    }
```

**Expected behavior**
`fooSet.equals(hashSet)` should return the same result as `hashSet.equals(fooSet)`

