@lprimak 

Lombok doesn't use APIs but internal classes and members. Standardising arbitrary AST transformations would be one of the most radical changes to the Java language. It would essentially mean that any library can change the meaning of Java code as it sees fit; it's more radical than adding macros. It would effectively turn Java into [Racket](https://racket-lang.org). The "compiler plugin API" (i.e. annotation processing) has been designed so that with any "plugin" the language that's accepted still conforms to the Java language specification (Lombok code obviously doesn't).

There's no doubt some people would love to see Java work like Racket, but there's also little doubt that it would change the nature of the language.

